# AGENT SYSTEM DIRECTIVES & IDE GOVERNANCE (.clinerules)
# Project: Provet Cloud ↔ Siigo Nube Integrator (DIAN Electronic Invoicing)

---

## 1. MANDATORY READ-FIRST PROTOCOL
Before writing, refactoring, or planning any code, you MUST inspect the following
root files. All seven live in the repo. **None of them may be duplicated into the
Project knowledge**: two unsynchronised copies already caused an agent to read a
stale `.clinerules` with a broken reference for several sessions.

1. `PROJECT_STATE.md` -> Its `## Current State` section is the single source of
   truth for verified state. The `Next Pending Task` lines further down are an
   append-only changelog, **not** live instructions.
2. `01_PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.md` -> Business logic, DIAN tax rules, API contract.
3. `2_AGENT_WORKFLOW_RULES.md` -> Token rules, atomic scope, agent matrix.
4. `03_UI_UX_DESIGN_SPEC.md` -> Strict clinical UI design constraints.
5. `EVIDENCIA_APIS.md` -> Observed evidence from Siigo and Provet.
   **Takes priority over official documentation**, under the class rule the
   document itself defines: API contracts (class A) always win; platform limits
   (class B) win only inside their stated validity window.
6. `API_SIIGO_REFERENCIA_COMPLETA.md` -> Captured official Siigo doc, endpoint by
   endpoint. Live source: `developers.siigo.com/docs/siigoapi/`.
   `developers.siigolatam.com` is dead — do not cite it.
7. `API_PROVET_CLOUD_REFERENCIA_COMPLETA.md` -> Captured official Provet doc.
   Live source: `developers.provetcloud.com`, plus the raw OpenAPI schema at
   `developers.provetcloud.com/restapi/0.1/openapi-schema-01.json`, which is
   authoritative over the captured markdown when the two disagree.

**`docs/audits/` is NOT part of this protocol.** It holds superseded audit reports
and the retired six-session plan, archived on 2026-09-10 for traceability only.
Every file there carries a header stating it is not a source of truth, and both
audits contain claims **falsified by live measurement** — listed in their headers.
Do not read them to decide what to do, and never execute anything from them. The
live backlog is `PROJECT_STATE.md` → `## Current State — Backlog Consolidado`.

---

## 2. OPERATIONAL MODES & EXECUTION FLOW

### Mode 1: PLAN MODE (Complex / Multi-file Tasks)
- When assigned a new Task, output a concise 5-step strategy FIRST.
- Specify target files, modified routes, Zod schemas, and test cases.
- DO NOT edit files until the user or system approves the plan.

### Mode 2: ACT & VERIFY MODE (Execution)
- Modify ONLY the target files listed under the session's frozen scope.
- Follow Test-Driven Development (TDD): write or update Zod schemas & Vitest unit
  tests before logic implementation, with the RED phase explicitly confirmed.
- Execute the mandatory **Verification Loop** before finalizing. All three green
  or no progress:
  1. `npx tsc --noEmit` (zero TypeScript errors).
  2. `npx vitest run` (full suite, 100% pass).
  3. `env -u NODE_ENV npx next build` (build completes).
- **There is no ESLint in this project.** `npm run lint` is an alias of
  `tsc --noEmit` and therefore identical to gate 1. It checks nothing new and is
  not a valid third gate. `next build` is.
- **The three gates do not see `vercel.json`.** A deleted or malformed header
  ships silently. That is why `src/test/vercelSecurityHeaders.test.ts` exists;
  generalise that shape-test pattern rather than removing it.
- If any command fails, fix the errors before updating `PROJECT_STATE.md`.

---

## 3. DOMAIN & INTEGRATION LAWS (PROVET ↔ SIIGO DIAN)

- **Mandatory API Headers:** All Siigo outgoing requests MUST include `Partner-Id`
  and a unique `Idempotency-Key` (max 30 chars, `/^[A-Za-z0-9]+$/` — no hyphens,
  so `crypto.randomUUID()` is not a valid key as-is).
- **A 500 from Siigo consumes the Idempotency-Key permanently.** Any retry must
  generate a fresh key.
- **Environment Safety:** Keep `stamp.send` set to `false` in Sandbox/Mock modes.
  Toggle to `true` strictly when running DIAN production flows.
  **EXCEPTION — credit notes:** `stamp.send` is ALWAYS `true` on credit notes,
  sandbox included, per DIAN Resolución 000042. Hardcoding it to `false` there is
  a legal bug, not a safe default.
- **Tolerance contract:** the schema tolerates extra fields (`.passthrough()`);
  the logic NEVER tolerates absent ones. A `transform` returning `cufe: ""` and
  `status: "Draft"` when the `stamp` carries no CUFE turns a DIAN-accepted invoice
  into a silent draft. If the field is missing, throw.
- **Runtime Validation:** All Provet input payloads and all outgoing JSON for
  `POST /v1/invoices` and `POST /v1/credit-notes` MUST pass strict Zod parsing
  before hitting the network.
- **Error Translation Layer:** Never expose raw API 500/429/400 stack traces to
  the UI. Map them to Spanish human-readable messages with fast-edit triggers.
- **Fail loudly, never silently.** A silent fallback is a bug, not a safe default.
  Documented and accepted exceptions: `login_rate_limit` (intentional fail-open).
- **`invoicerow.sum_total` is read verbatim, never recalculated.** Reading it
  verbatim does NOT authorise discarding rows with `sum_total <= 0`: negative rows
  exist in the live tenant and dropping them produces silent over-invoicing.
- **A Provet credit note is a new invoice record** with `credit_note: true` and
  `consultation: null`. Neither the sign of `sum_total` nor the sign of `quantity`
  identifies a credit: only `invoice.credit_note` and `invoicerow.credited_invoicerow` do.
- **Invoice dates are computed in `America/Bogota`**, never from a raw
  `new Date().toISOString()` (that is UTC and shifts the date at night).
- **Never hardcode account-specific IDs** (document type, seller). They come from
  `catalog_mapping`, throwing `MissingEmissionSettingError` /
  `MissingCreditNoteSettingError` when absent.

---

## 4. UI/UX CLINICAL CONSTRAINTS
- Strictly enforce `03_UI_UX_DESIGN_SPEC.md`.
- Palette: Cool Grey (`#F4F6F8`), Pure White (`#FFFFFF`), Clinical Blue (`#0052CC`), Slate Text (`#1A202C`).
- Layout: Dense tabular display, compact padding (`p-2` to `p-4`), max border-radius `rounded-md` (6px).
- Strictly PROHIBITED: Glowing neon colors, floating cards with massive drop shadows, oversized rounded corners (`rounded-2xl`/`3xl`), and generic SaaS illustrations.

---

## 5. ZERO SMALL-TALK DIRECTIVE & OUTPUT FORMAT

Do NOT print greetings, conversational confirmations, or filler text.

All task completion responses MUST strictly adhere to this format:
1. **Technical Summary:** 3 lines max summarizing the code changes.
2. **Complete files, never partial diffs**, each with its full path from the repo
   root. A partial diff already caused one route handler to overwrite another and
   broke invoice emission in production undetected.
3. **Updated PROJECT_STATE.md:** Markdown snippet reflecting the completed task,
   modified files, and the next pending task.

## CODE EFFICIENCY & REUSE LAWS
- REUSE BEFORE CREATING: Always search `/src` for existing helpers, interfaces, or mappers before writing new code. Reinventing existing utilities is strictly forbidden.
- ALGORITHMIC SIMPLICITY: Prefer functional, pure transformations (Zod / native JS methods). Maximum complexity allowed for data transformation is O(n).
- FILE SIZE LIMIT — **single authoritative definition.** No single file under
  `/src/services`, `/src/mappers` or `/src/components` shall exceed **150 raw
  lines** (`wc -l`, blanks and comments included). `/src/app` is explicitly OUT OF
  SCOPE: those are composition pages and the limit is counterproductive there.
  This supersedes every other wording of the rule in the repo. Under it there are
  currently **17 violations**, deliberately not remediated — see the backlog.
  Do not reinterpret this rule to make work pass a gate.
- ZERO DUPLICATION: UI components must NEVER perform raw data mapping or direct API calls. Use existing `/services` and `/mappers` exclusively.
- `src/mocks/` is NOT a test artifact — production files import it.
- `ts-prune` reports false positives for exports feeding `export type X = z.infer<...>`.
